{
    "background_story": "Marigold was a lovable pig who lived on a small farm surrounded by rolling hills and lush green pastures. She loved nothing more than indulging in the sweetest, most succulent fruits and vegetables that grew in the farm's gardens. As a result, Marigold had a tendency to overindulge, and her corpulence became the stuff of local legend. Despite her size, she was a gentle soul with a heart of gold, always willing to lend a listening ear or a comforting nuzzle to her fellow farm animals. Marigold's love of food often led to comical misadventures, such as getting stuck in the farm's narrow gates or requiring a team of animals to push her up the hill to her favorite snacking spot. Her jovial nature and infectious laughter made her a beloved fixture on the farm, and her corpulence only added to her charm.",
